## Rules of thumb (Tbilisi @ 41.7° N on 22 Mar)

| Facade direction | Hours (Mar 22) | Pass-by-itself? |
|---|---|---|
| North (0°)          | 0.2 h          | NO  |
| North-East (45°)    | 3.0 h          | YES |
| East (90°)          | 6.0 h          | YES |
| South-East (135°)   | 8.9 h          | YES |
| South (180°)        | 11.8 h         | YES |
| South-West (225°)   | 8.9 h          | YES |
| West (270°)         | 6.1 h          | YES |
| North-West (315°)   | 3.0 h          | YES |

So **any window not within ±45° of due-North** passes the СНиП §6
threshold on the equinox.

## Combined with the `K-coefficients` (rule 06)

If insolation fails, before redesigning the unit consider:

1. Increasing the side-yard distance (more daylight reaches lower
   floors) — `h` rule from `06-grg-coefficients.mdc`.
2. Re-orientation of the block (rotation in plan).
3. Adding a balcony cut-out or a corner-window detail to open up to
   the south.

## Future work (v2)

- **Shading by neighbours**. Currently we treat the window as if it has
  open sky on its exposed side. A ray-trace against `xref_shenobebi`
  (existing buildings) is needed for a full GRG-grade study; see the
  reference `archilume` / FreeCAD-Solar / NREL SAM tools listed in
  `12-external-libraries.mdc`.
- **Per-window** orientation instead of per-facade. We currently take
  every exterior polygon edge as a potential window. To upgrade, dump
  the window-block INSERT entities from the DWG (already in
  `walls.json`'s INSERT list — not yet wired) and use their rotation
  angle as the facing direction.
- **Glazing-to-floor ratio cross-check.** Combine with СНиП §5
  daylight-factor (`window_area >= 1/8 * room_area`, rule 09).
